messages:
ajay: Hey team — customer reported failing tool invocation to billing.create_invoice. They get a 400 with schema_validation errors. Posting customer payload + server error below.

ajay: REQUEST (from customer SDK v2.1.0):
```json
{"tool":"billing.create_invoice","args":{"customerId":"cust_123","amount":"1000","currency":"usd","promo":"SUMMER"}}
```

ajay: SERVER RESPONSE (gateway):
```json
{
  "status": 400,
  "error": {
    "type": "schema_validation",
    "message": "Request body failed JSON schema validation",
    "details": [
      {"path": "", "message": "Missing required property: customer_id"},
      {"path": "/amount", "message": "Expected integer but got string"},
      {"path": "", "message": "Additional properties are not allowed: promo"}
    ]
  }
}
```

ben: Ouch. Customer says it worked yesterday. They did a quick upgrade of our SDK from 2.0.9 -> 2.1.0 earlier today.

maria: @ajay thanks. quick theory: server schema changed to require snake_case customer_id and strict integer amount. SDK 2.1.0 probably started sending camelCase and strings for amounts. Also we enabled additionalProperties: false on that tool schema last week which would reject promo.

maria: Can you repro with curl from our support env? If so include exact curl + headers and I'll try a shim.

ajay: repro steps (curl):
```
curl -X POST "https://api.redwood.example/v1/tools/invoke" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"tool":"billing.create_invoice","args":{"customerId":"cust_123","amount":"1000","currency":"usd","promo":"SUMMER"}}'
```

ajay: Repro'd locally on staging, same error.

maria: ok. short-term options:
- server-side shim: map customerId -> customer_id, coerce amount string -> int, strip unknown props (promo) OR
- quick SDK patch to send snake_case and integers OR
- relax additionalProperties for that tool schema (risky)

maria: I'll open a tiny gateway hotfix to transform incoming args for billing.create_invoice: map camelCase to snake_case and coerce numeric strings. That will restore compatibility while we coordinate an official SDK release.

dave: can we log telemetry of how many requests contain promo or camelCase fields? want to estimate blast radius.

ci-bot: noted: creating ticket RW-6843 (gateway: billing args compat shim) and CI job to test coercion. Assigned to maria.

maria: quick patch snippet (node express middleware) to run in gateway:
```js
function normalizeBillingArgs(args) {
  if (args.customerId && !args.customer_id) {
    args.customer_id = args.customerId;
    delete args.customerId;
  }
  if (typeof args.amount === 'string') {
    const n = parseInt(args.amount, 10);
    if (!Number.isNaN(n)) args.amount = n;
  }
  // drop unknown promocodes
  if (args.promo) delete args.promo;
  return args;
}
```

maria: Pushed branch, running unit tests. Will push hotfix to staging after smoke tests.

ajay: Customer updated: they can wait for a server-side hotfix. They prefer not to downgrade SDK.

ben: Please add a note to customer that we tolerate camelCase for 48 hours and will coordinate SDK patch; also capture affected tenant IDs.

maria: will do. logging added to RW-6843 to capture example payloads and tenant ids for next 24h.

ajay: thx. marking as customer-impacting.

maria: hotfix deployed to staging, smoke looks good. planning promo discard + coercion to main after 30m.

ben: :thumbsup: coordinate comms with CS.

ajay: I'll update ticket and message the customer once prod deploy is green.

maria: follow-ups: we should add a test that fails if SDK and server disagree on field casing/number types. I'll add to integration suite.

ajay: closing loop once prod change is live. thanks everyone.
